  title: 'Taxes in Singapore (Present Day) '
  info: "Singapore has a low tax environment, making it attractive for businesses
    and individuals. The personal income tax rate is progressive, ranging from 0%
    to 22%, while corporate tax is capped at 17%. There is no capital gains tax or
    estate duty. Goods and Services Tax (GST) is set at 9% from 2024, affecting daily
    expenses. The government\u2019s tax policies support economic growth while maintaining
    a high standard of public services, including infrastructure, healthcare, and
    education.  "
